      "id": "GENUS_PELECANUS",
      "name": "Pelecanus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Pelicans — unmistakable waterbirds with a massive throat pouch (gular sac) used to scoop fish from the water. The pouch can hold up to 13 litres and is drained before swallowing. Despite their heavy appearance, pelicans are graceful in flight, soaring in formation with slow, powerful wingbeats. They have the largest wingspans of any freshwater bird, reaching 3.5 metres.",
      "lineage": "Pelicans",
